@* The field posts a URL, not bytes. The file goes to Action by fetch the moment it is chosen,
   and what the form carries is the hidden input holding what came back — so this form is an
   ordinary form rather than a multipart one, and a picture survives a validation failure that
   re-renders the page. *@
<form method="post" action="/products" class="w-full max-w-sm">
    <AntiforgeryToken />
    <FieldGroup>
        <Field>
            <FieldLabel For="cover">Cover image</FieldLabel>
            <FileUpload id="cover" Name="cover" Action="/uploads"
                        Hint="JPEG, PNG or WebP · up to 8MB" />
            <FieldDescription>Dropped, chosen, or pasted from a file manager.</FieldDescription>
        </Field>
    </FieldGroup>
</form>
